{"id": "holmes", "title": "The Case of the Blue Ink", "level": "B1", "scenes": [{"title": "A Visitor at Baker Street", "text": "One foggy morning in London, a young woman named Emily Carter knocked on the door of 221B Baker Street. She looked tired and worried. “Mr Holmes,” she said, “someone has stolen my father’s gold watch. It was the last gift he gave me before he died.” Sherlock Holmes put down his violin and asked her to sit by the fire. Doctor Watson, his loyal friend, took out his notebook and began to write.", "img": "scene1.webp", "para": 1, "fx": ["fog", "fire", "dust", "vignette"], "fire": [98, 42], "focus": [55, 40], "slow": true}, {"title": "Three Suspects", "text": "Emily explained that the watch had disappeared from her desk the night before. Only three people had been in the house: her cousin Robert, the old cook Mrs Bell, and a young gardener called Tom. “The window was closed and the door was locked,” she said. “Nobody could come in from outside.” Holmes listened carefully with his eyes closed. Then he stood up quickly. “Watson, get your coat. We must visit the house at once.”", "img": "scene2.webp", "para": 2, "fx": ["fire", "dust", "vignette"], "fire": [98, 45], "focus": [55, 45], "slow": true}, {"title": "The Blue Spot", "text": "At the house, Holmes examined the desk with his magnifying glass. He found a small spot of blue ink on the wooden floor.", "img": "scene3.webp", "para": 3, "fx": ["dust", "glow", "vignette"], "glow": [7, 14], "focus": [50, 80]}, {"title": "Ink on His Fingers", "text": "Then he asked to see the hands of everyone in the house. The cook’s hands smelled of bread, and the gardener’s hands were covered in soil. But there was blue ink on Robert’s fingers, although he said that he had not written anything for days.", "img": "scene4.webp", "para": 3, "fx": ["dust", "glow", "vignette"], "glow": [73, 17], "focus": [82, 40]}, {"title": "The Truth", "text": "“You took the watch,” Holmes said calmly, “because you needed money to pay